## 3. Three module harnesses

Use locking JST-XH connections at the main PCB and soldered, strain-relieved ends at the modules. The encoder and power switch mount directly on the main PCB.

| Qty to buy | Manufacturer | Exact part number | Use | DigiKey |
|---:|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | JST | XHP-2 | Housing mating with J2 | [Buy](https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/jst-sales-america-inc/XHP-2/555485) |
| 2 | JST | XHP-4 | Housings mating with J3 and J4 | [Buy](https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/jst-sales-america-inc/XHP-4/683353) |
| 5 | JST | ASXHSXH22K305 | 304.8 mm, 22 AWG, black, socket-to-socket XH pre-crimped leads | [Buy](https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/jst-sales-america-inc/ASXHSXH22K305/6684932) |

Cut each pre-crimped lead at its midpoint: five leads yield ten approximately 152 mm tails, each retaining one factory crimp. Populate 2 + 4 + 4 housing positions. Strip and solder only the cut ends. No loose crimp contacts, crimp tool, or bulk wire spool is required for these harnesses.

Label both ends of every black wire before insertion. Pin order is defined by the mating header's numbered pads, not by looking at the front of the cable housing. Verify with continuity testing. Reserve room for these harness lengths in the enclosure; shorten the solder ends if necessary.

## 4. Fixed build settings

- Charger: Adafruit 4410, 100 mA; leave the 500 mA jumper OPEN.
- Battery: Adafruit 1578 only for this build; supplied protection and connector remain intact.
- USB: standard 5 V USB source with a USB-C-ended cable; USB-A-to-C and USB-C-to-C are supported by the charger's documented circuitry. No PD trigger or high-voltage supply.
- Operation: S1 OFF before USB insertion, and USB removed before S1 ON.
- Regulator: C1 and C2 are ceramic shunt capacitors, not series elements.
- AREF: C5 to GND only; no direct connection to +3.3V.
- Encoder: external pull-ups plus RC filters; firmware must use INPUT, not INPUT_PULLUP.
- I2C: populate R2/R3; use 100 kHz and short harnesses. A3's onboard 10 kohm pull-ups remain installed. Check combined bus loading and rise time with A2 connected before releasing the PCB.
- U1: internal 8 MHz, no crystal or socket.
- S1: pin 2 common, pin 1 switched output, pin 3 unconnected.

## 5. PCB and release notes

- Use `Package_TO_SOT_THT:TO-92_Inline_Wide` as the starting point for U2's 2.54 mm pad spacing; verify numbered pads and lead forming against the actual package.
- S1 terminal spacing is 2.50 mm. The manufacturer's drawing identifies pin 2 as common.
- SW1 needs the horizontal/rear-facing, switched PEC11R footprint. Match A/B/C and the two push-switch contacts explicitly; do not reuse the old custom symbol's numeric mapping.
- All capacitors are nonpolarized. Match each footprint to the purchased part's actual lead spacing.
- Add copper test pads and four mounting holes in the PCB design; these are not additional purchased electronic components.
- This BOM covers the electronic assembly and its three harnesses. PCB fabrication, enclosure, mounting hardware, knob, diffuser, insulation/strain-relief supplies, programmer, and external USB source/cable are outside the electronics purchasing count. Their mechanical dimensions must be settled before PCB/enclosure fabrication.
- Existing firmware is NOT yet compatible with this wiring: see the manual's mandatory firmware section before powering a programmed unit.

## 6. Charging evidence

- [Adafruit 4410 product documentation](https://www.adafruit.com/product/4410): assembled USB-C charger, VBAT/GND breakout, default 100 mA charging.
- [Adafruit charger schematic downloads, PID 4410](https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-microlipo-and-minilipo-battery-chargers/downloads): USB-C CC1 and CC2 each have their own 5.1 kohm resistor to GND. The charge-programming resistor is 10 kohm with the rate jumper open.
- [Adafruit 1578 battery documentation](https://www.adafruit.com/product/1578): integrated protection, matched connector polarity, and charging at 500 mA or less. The selected 100 mA rate is 0.2C.
- [Adafruit 4681 pinouts](https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-bh1750-ambient-light-sensor/pinouts): VIN accepts 3-5 V, SDA/SCL have 10 kohm pull-ups, and default address is 0x23.

These sources establish design compatibility, not a completed charging or hardware test. Perform the manual's acceptance checks on the purchased assemblies.
